  "body": "Adds a dependency-free Python exporter and manual Actions workflow for #60. Issues, PR conversations/reviews, releases, tags, root-README text and GitHub-hosted media are preserved as JSON, readable pages and a checksummed URL-to-file manifest. The workflow commits the dump to a dedicated archive branch. Reruns reuse verified files; missing media and exhausted budgets remain explicit failures.\r\n\r\n**Hosted validation passed:** https://github.com/Manntouu/THE-ERROR-IS-THE-MESSAGE/actions/runs/34750105125\r\n**Resulting archive:** https://github.com/Manntouu/THE-ERROR-IS-THE-MESSAGE/tree/39c82de8ca56deb8d78a7d0e944513d802f126e1/repository-dump\r\n\r\nThe successful run exported 60 issues, 6 PRs, 168 conversation comments, 4 releases/tags and 399 attachment URLs with zero failures. Its 400 part references resolve to 342 unique stored files after deduplication. Every asset's size/SHA-256 and all 342 remote Git media-blob IDs match independently verified local files. All 14 tests passed.\r\n\r\nThe archive index and issue #60 were exercised in a browser. The manual workflow controls were opened and filled at a 390px phone-sized viewport; actual dispatch was from desktop, with no physical-handset claim. See tools/REPOSITORY_ARCHIVE.md and tools/VALIDATION.md for reproduction and evidence.\r\n\r\nScope excludes deleted/inaccessible content, full edit histories, separate Discussions, wikis, projects, Actions artifacts and Git history; snapshots are non-atomic.\r\n\r\n€100 bounty claim, subject to maintainer acceptance and payment confirmation. AI-assisted implementation and validation by Codex, authorized for @Manntouu.\r\n",
